	"department": "LATIN",
	"description": [
		"Students expand their knowledge of Latin by exploring the diverse and creative literature of the Middle Ages, ca. 300-1500 CE. This course emphasizes the role of Latin as the language of religious life in Medieval Europe. Topics encountered typically include scripture, pilgrims, relics, miracles, saints, crusaders, monastics, and the black death. Offered annually in the spring semester. Also counts toward ancient studies, and medieval studies majors, and concentrations in linguistic studies and international relations. Prerequisite: LATIN 231 or equivalent."
	],
